tab win | Windows | window

sub boot | Boot & logon

tweak win.logon | login | rec
  name  Faster sign-in
  desc  Shows the desktop without waiting for the sign-in animation timeout and stops logon and startup scripts from blocking the shell.
  R     CV\Policies\System | DelayedDesktopSwitchTimeout | d:0 | -
  R     CV\Policies\System | RunLogonScriptSync | d:0 | -
  R     NT\Winlogon | RunLogonScriptSync | d:0 | -
  R     NT\Winlogon | RunStartupScriptSync | d:0 | -
  R     CV\Policies\System | EnableFirstLogonAnimation | d:0 | -
  R     UCV\Explorer\Serialize | StartupDelayInMSec | d:0 | -

tweak win.oobe | person_add | rec
  name  Setup screens for new accounts off
  desc  Skips the online account, EULA, Wi-Fi, OEM registration, privacy and Cortana voice screens when a new user is set up, defaults the privacy choices to off and allows setup without internet.
  OOBE  HideOnlineAccountScreens=1 HideEULAPage=1 HideWirelessSetupInOOBE=1 ProtectYourPC=3 DisablePrivacyExperience=1 HideOEMRegistrationScreen=1 EnableCortanaVoice=0 DisableVoice=1
  R     CV\OOBE | BypassNRO | d:1 | -

tweak win.faststart | restart_alt | rec
  name  Fast startup off
  desc  Turns off hybrid shutdown, so every shutdown is a clean one. Fixes drivers and updates that only apply after a real restart.
  R     CC\Session Manager\Power | HiberbootEnabled | d:0 | d:1
  R     PW\System | HiberbootEnabled | d:0 | -

tweak win.autochk | fact_check | risk2
  name  Boot disk check off
  desc  Removes the countdown before a scheduled disk check and skips the automatic check of drive C at boot. You can still run chkdsk yourself.
  R     CC\Session Manager | AutoChkTimeOut | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Session Manager | BootExecute | m:autocheck autochk /k:C * | m:autocheck autochk *

tweak win.bootmenu | menu_open | rec
  name  Classic boot menu
  desc  Uses the text boot menu, so F8 opens Safe Mode and the other startup options again.
  BCD   /set bootmenupolicy Legacy
  off:
  BCD   /set bootmenupolicy Standard

tweak win.verbose | subject | rec
  name  Detailed status messages
  desc  Shows what Windows is doing during start, sign-in and shutdown instead of "Please wait".
  R     CV\Policies\System | VerboseStatus | d:1 | -

tweak win.lkg | history | rec
  name  Last Known Good boot option
  desc  Lets Windows fall back to the last configuration that booted, when a driver or setting breaks startup.
  BCD   /set lastknowngood yes
  off:
  BCD-  /deletevalue lastknowngood

tweak win.utc | schedule
  name  Hardware clock in UTC
  desc  Treats the motherboard clock as UTC, like Linux does. Only switch this on if you dual-boot, or the clock will be off by your time zone.
  R     CC\TimeZoneInformation | RealTimeIsUniversal | d:1 | -

sub explorer | Explorer

tweak win.previews | preview | rec
  name  Faster hover previews
  desc  Shows taskbar thumbnails and desktop peek after 250 ms instead of the default delay.
  R     CV\Explorer\Advanced | DesktopLivePreviewHoverTime | d:250 | -
  R     CV\Explorer\Advanced | ThumbnailLivePreviewHoverTime | d:250 | -

tweak win.newapps | new_releases | rec
  name  New app highlights off
  desc  Stops Start from highlighting and notifying you about newly installed apps.
  R     CV\Explorer\Advanced | Start_NotifyNewApps | d:0 | -

tweak win.netthumbs | image_not_supported | rec
  name  Thumbs.db on network folders off
  desc  Stops Explorer from writing hidden thumbnail cache files into shared network folders.
  R     PW\Explorer | DisableThumbsDBOnNetworkFolders | d:1 | -

tweak win.cloudrecent | cloud_off | rec
  name  Cloud files in Recent off
  desc  Hides recent files from your Microsoft 365 and OneDrive cloud account in Explorer's Home and Start.
  R     PW\Explorer | DisableGraphRecentItems | d:1 | -

tweak win.shellfast | speed | rec
  name  Shell latency
  desc  Shuts idle COM servers down after 1 second, copies files with buffered I/O, turns off catalog and Win32k verbose counters, stops watching network folders for remote changes and skips push-notification setup at startup.
  R     CV\CapabilityAccessManager | ComServerShutdownDelayMs | d:1000 | -
  R     PW\System | CopyFileBufferedSynchronousIo | d:1 | -
  R     M\Cryptography\CatalogDB | EnablePerformanceCounters | d:0 | -
  R     NT\Windows\Win32kWPP\Parameters | VerboseOn | d:0 | -
  R     CV\Policies\Explorer | NoRemoteChangeNotify | d:1 | -
  R     CV\Policies\Explorer | NoRemoteRecursiveEvents | d:1 | -
  R     CV\PushNotifications | InitializePlatformOnStartup | d:0 | -
  R     CV\Audio | AudioHealthMonitorLimit | d:0 | -

tweak win.explorerfast | bolt | rec
  name  Explorer speed
  desc  Runs folder windows in their own process, stops Explorer from crawling the network for printers and shares, from guessing each folder's type and from scanning disks for low space, and resolves shortcuts without slow network lookups.
  R     UCV\Explorer\Advanced | SeparateProcess | d:1 | -
  R     UCV\Explorer\Advanced | NoNetCrawling | d:1 | -
  R     HKCU\Software\Classes\Local Settings\Software\Microsoft\Windows\Shell\Bags\AllFolders\Shell | FolderType | s:NotSpecified | -
  R     UCV\Explorer | MultipleInvokePromptMinimum | s:100 | -
  R     UCV\Policies\Explorer | LinkResolveIgnoreLinkInfo | d:1 | -
  R     UCV\Policies\Explorer | NoLowDiskSpaceChecks | d:1 | -
  R     UPW\Explorer | DisableThumbsDBOnNetworkFolders | d:1 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop | LowLevelHooksTimeout | s:1000 | -

tweak win.storeopen | storefront | rec
  name  "Look for an app in the Store" off
  desc  Opening an unknown file type no longer offers to search the Store or the web for an app.
  R     CV\Policies\Explorer | NoInternetOpenWith | d:1 | -
  R     PW\Explorer | NoUseStoreOpenWith | d:1 | -

tweak win.longpaths | straighten | rec
  name  Long file paths
  desc  Lets apps that support it use file paths longer than 260 characters.
  R     CC\FileSystem | LongPathsEnabled | d:1 | d:0

tweak win.hiddentasks | visibility | rec
  name  Show hidden scheduled tasks
  desc  Makes Task Scheduler list the tasks Windows normally hides.
  R     M\SchedulingAgent | ViewHiddenTasks | d:1 | -

tweak win.psopen | terminal | risk2
  name  Run .ps1 on double-click
  desc  Makes PowerShell scripts run when you open them and adds "Run as administrator" to their menu. Convenient, but a downloaded script runs as soon as you open it.
  R     HKCR\Microsoft.PowerShellScript.1\Shell\Open\Command |  | x:"%SystemRoot%\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe" "%1" | x:"%SystemRoot%\System32\notepad.exe" "%1"
  R     HKCR\Microsoft.PowerShellScript.1\Shell\RunAs | HasLUAShield | s: | -
  R     HKCR\Microsoft.PowerShellScript.1\Shell\RunAs\Command |  | x:"%SystemRoot%\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe" "%1" | -

sub power | Power & shutdown

tweak win.shutdown | power_off | rec
  name  Faster shutdown
  desc  Gives hung apps and services 5 seconds to close at shutdown instead of waiting much longer.
  R     HKU\.DEFAULT\Control Panel\Desktop | WaitToKillTimeout | s:5000 | -
  R     HKU\.DEFAULT\Control Panel\Desktop | CriticalAppShutdownTimeout | d:5000 | -
  R     HKU\.DEFAULT\Control Panel\Desktop | CriticalAppShutdownCleanupTimeout | d:5000 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop | WaitToKillAppTimeout | s:2000 | -
  R     SYS\Control | WaitToKillServiceTimeout | s:2000 | s:5000
  R     CC\Session Manager | TaskhostTimeout | d:2000 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop | HungAppTimeout | s:2000 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop | AutoEndTasks | s:1 | -

sub input | Keyboard, sound & accessibility

tweak win.stickykeys | accessibility_new | rec
  name  Accessibility shortcut pop-ups off
  desc  Stops Sticky Keys, Filter Keys, Toggle Keys, Mouse Keys and High Contrast from popping up when you press Shift five times or hold keys in games, and stops Narrator starting with Win+Enter.
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\StickyKeys | Flags | s:506 | s:510
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\Keyboard Response | Flags | s:122 | s:126
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\ToggleKeys | Flags | s:58 | s:62
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\MouseKeys | Flags | s:130 | s:62
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\HighContrast | Flags | s:4194 | s:126
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility | Sound on Activation | d:0 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility | Warning Sounds | s:0 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Accessibility\SlateLaunch | LaunchAT | s:0 | -
  R     UM\Ease of Access | selfscan | s:0 | -
  R     UM\Ease of Access | selfvoice | s:0 | -
  R     UM\Narrator\NoRoam | WinEnterLaunchEnabled | d:0 | -

tweak win.keyboard | keyboard | rec
  name  Keyboard shortcuts & repeat
  desc  Uses the shortest key repeat delay, turns off the Alt+Shift and Ctrl+Shift layout switching hotkeys and keeps Print Screen as a plain screenshot key.
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Keyboard | KeyboardDelay | d:0 | s:1
  R     HKCU\Keyboard Layout\Toggle | Hotkey | s:3 | s:1
  R     HKCU\Keyboard Layout\Toggle | Language Hotkey | s:3 | s:1
  R     HKCU\Keyboard Layout\Toggle | Layout Hotkey | s:3 | s:2
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Keyboard | PrintScreenKeyForSnippingEnabled | d:0 | -

tweak win.sound | volume_down | rec
  name  Sounds & ducking off
  desc  Stops Windows from lowering other audio during calls, turns off notification sounds and system beeps, and hides disconnected audio devices in the sound panel.
  R     UM\Multimedia\Audio | UserDuckingPreference | d:3 | -
  R     UCV\Notifications\Settings | NOC_GLOBAL_SETTING_ALLOW_NOTIFICATION_SOUND | d:0 | -
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Sound | Beep | s:no | s:yes
  R     HKCU\Control Panel\Mouse | Beep | s:No | -
  R     UM\Multimedia\Audio\DeviceCpl | ShowDisconnectedDevices | d:0 | -
  R     UM\Multimedia\Audio\DeviceCpl | ShowHiddenDevices | d:0 | -

tweak win.usbnotify | usb | rec
  name  USB warnings off
  desc  Hides the "USB device not recognised" and weak charger notifications, which often show for devices that work fine.
  R     UM\Shell\USB | NotifyOnUsbErrors | s:0 | -
  R     UM\Shell\USB | NotifyOnWeakCharger | s:0 | -

tweak win.terminal | terminal | rec
  name  Terminal as default console
  desc  Opens Command Prompt and PowerShell in Windows Terminal instead of the old console window.
  R     HKCU\Console\%%Startup | DelegationConsole | s:{B23D10C0-E52E-411E-9D5B-C09FDF709C7D} | -
  R     HKCU\Console\%%Startup | DelegationTerminal | s:{B23D10C0-E52E-411E-9D5B-C09FDF709C7D} | -

tweak win.powermenu | power_settings_new | rec
  name  Power menu options
  desc  Shows Sleep in the power menu and lets you shut down from the sign-in screen without signing in.
  R     CV\Explorer\FlyoutMenuSettings | ShowSleepOption | d:1 | -
  R     CV\Policies\System | ShutdownWithoutLogon | d:1 | -

tweak win.hibernate | mode_standby | desktop
  name  Hibernation off
  desc  Turns hibernation off on desktops and deletes hiberfil.sys, which frees space the size of a good part of your RAM. Laptops keep it so a dead battery does not lose your work.
  R     CC\Power | HibernateEnabled | d:0 | d:1
  R     CC\Power | AllowHibernate | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Power | HibernateEnabledDefault | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Session Manager\Power | HibernateEnabled | d:0 | -
  R     CV\Explorer\FlyoutMenuSettings | ShowHibernateOption | d:0 | -
  C     powercfg /hibernate off
  off:
  C     powercfg /hibernate on

tweak win.modernsb | bedtime | desktop reboot
  name  Modern Standby off
  desc  Switches desktops back to classic S3 sleep instead of Modern Standby, which keeps the network and background tasks running while asleep. Skipped on PCs with a battery.
  R     CC\Power | PlatformAoAcOverride | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Power | CsEnabled | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Power | MSDisabled | d:1 | -

sub crash | Crashes

tweak win.crash | report | rec
  name  Crash dumps & blue screens
  desc  Keeps a small memory dump instead of a full one, shows the stop code details and stays on the blue screen instead of restarting, so you can read what failed.
  R     CC\CrashControl | CrashDumpEnabled | d:3 | d:7
  R     CC\CrashControl | AutoReboot | d:0 | d:1
  R     CC\CrashControl | DisplayParameters | d:1 | -
  R     CC\CrashControl | AlwaysKeepMemoryDump | d:0 | -
  R     CC\CrashControl | SendAlert | d:0 | -
  R     CC\CrashControl | LogEvent | d:0 | d:1
  R     CC\CrashControl\StorageTelemetry | DeviceDumpEnabled | d:0 | -
  R     CC\CrashControl | DisableEmoticon | d:1 | -

sub security | Security

tweak win.printnight | print_lock | rec
  name  Point and Print hardening
  desc  Only administrators can install printer drivers, and Windows always warns before it does. Closes the PrintNightmare hole.
  R     PM\Windows NT\Printers\PointAndPrint | RestrictDriverInstallationToAdministrators | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows NT\Printers\PointAndPrint | NoWarningNoElevationOnInstall | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows NT\Printers\PointAndPrint | UpdatePromptSettings | d:0 | -

tweak win.dcom | admin_panel_settings | rec
  name  System hardening
  desc  Requires packet integrity for remote DCOM activation, blocks unencrypted Basic auth in the WinRM client, stops installers from always running elevated and disables the old AT task command.
  R     M\Ole\AppCompat | RequireIntegrityActivationAuthenticationLevel | d:1 | -
  R     NT\Schedule\Configuration | EnableAt | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WinRM\Client | AllowBasic | d:0 | -
  R     PW\Installer | AlwaysInstallElevated | d:0 | -
  R     CC\Lsa | RestrictAnonymous | d:1 | d:0
  R     SV\LanmanServer\Parameters | RestrictNullSessAccess | d:1 | -

tweak win.dma | cable | risk2 reboot
  name  Kernel DMA protection
  desc  Blocks external Thunderbolt and USB4 devices that do not support DMA remapping until you sign in. Safer against DMA attacks, but some docks stop working.
  R     PW\Kernel DMA Protection | DeviceEnumerationPolicy | d:0 | -

tweak win.filehistory | history | rec
  name  File History off
  desc  Turns off File History backups. Leave it on if you back up to an external drive with it.
  R     PW\FileHistory | Disabled | d:1 | -

tweak win.firewall | security | rec
  name  Firewall profiles
  desc  Keeps the firewall on for every network type, blocks unsolicited inbound connections, allows outbound, stops unicast replies to multicast and hides the "app was blocked" pop-ups.
  FWP   StandardProfile PublicProfile PrivateProfile
  R     PM\WindowsFirewall\%P | EnableFirewall | d:1 | -
  R     PM\WindowsFirewall\%P | DefaultInboundAction | d:2 | -
  R     PM\WindowsFirewall\%P | DefaultOutboundAction | d:0 | -
  R     PM\WindowsFirewall\%P | DisableFirewallNotifications | d:1 | -
  R     PM\WindowsFirewall\%P | DisableUnicastResponseToMulticast | d:1 | -

tweak win.defender | shield | risk3 reboot ti
  name  Microsoft Defender
  desc  Choose how much of Defender stays. Disable turns off real-time protection, cloud reporting, sample upload, notifications and its loggers through policy. Remove deletes the services, drivers and files. Turn off Tamper Protection in Windows Security first.
  opt   keep | Keep (tuned)
  K-    PM\Windows Defender
  K-    PM\Microsoft Antimalware
  R     M\Windows Defender\Features | TamperProtection | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Scan | AvgCPULoadFactor | d:20 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Scan | LowCpuPriority | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Scan | ScanOnlyIfIdle | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Scan | DisableCatchupQuickScan | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Scan | DisableCatchupFullScan | d:1 | -
  SVCS  2 | WinDefend:2 SecurityHealthService:2 wscsvc:2 MsSecCore:2 MsSecWfp:2 MsSecFlt:2 SgrmBroker:2 wtd:2 webthreatdefusersvc:2 webthreatdefsvc:2
  SVCS  3 | WdNisSvc:3 Sense:3 MDCoreSvc:3 SgrmAgent:3 MDCoreSvc_* webthreatdefusersvc_*
  R     CV\Run | SecurityHealth | x:%windir%\system32\SecurityHealthSystray.exe | -
  AREG  Microsoft.SecHealthUI
  T     enable \Microsoft\Windows\Windows Defender\
  opt   disable | Disable
  R     M\Windows Defender\Features | TamperProtection | d:0 | -
  R     M\RemovalTools\MpGears | HeartbeatTrackingIndex | d:0 | -
  R     M\RemovalTools\MpGears | SpyNetReportingLocation | m: | -
  SPV   windowsdefender
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisableAntiSpyware | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisableAntiVirus | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | AllowFastServiceStartup | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | ServiceKeepAlive | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableRealtimeMonitoring | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableBehaviorMonitoring | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableScanOnRealtimeEnable | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableIOAVProtection | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableOnAccessProtection | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableScriptScanning | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Spynet | SpynetReporting | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Spynet | SubmitSamplesConsent | d:2 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Reporting | DisableGenericReports | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Signature Updates | DisableScheduledSignatureUpdateOnBattery | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\SmartScreen | ConfigureAppInstallControlEnabled | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\SmartScreen | ConfigureAppInstallControl | s:Anywhere | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\MpEngine | MpCloudBlockLevel | d:2 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableRealtimeMonitoring | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender\Features | VerifiedAndReputablePolicyState | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender\Spynet | DisableBlockAtFirstSeen | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender Security Center\Systray | HideSystray | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Notifications | DisableNotifications | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Virus and threat protection | VirusThreatProtectionsArea | d:0 | -
  R     CC\WMI\Autologger\DefenderApiLogger | Start | d:0 | d:1
  R     CC\WMI\Autologger\DefenderAuditLogger | Start | d:0 | d:1
  FEAT  Windows-Defender-ApplicationGuard
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Windows Defender\
  R     M\Windows Defender\Features | TamperProtectionSource | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableBehaviorMonitoring | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender\Real-Time Protection | DisableOnAccessProtection | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender Security Center\Virus and threat protection | SummaryNotificationDisabled | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender Security Center\Virus and threat protection | NoActionNotificationDisabled | d:1 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender Security Center\Virus and threat protection | FilesBlockedNotificationDisabled | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\Controlled Folder Access | EnableControlledFolderAccess | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\Network Protection | EnableNetworkProtection | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisallowExploitProtectionOverride | d:1 | -
  R     CV\Explorer | AicEnabled | s:Anywhere | -
  R     M\Security Center | FirewallDisableNotify | d:1 | -
  R     M\Security Center | AntiVirusDisableNotify | d:1 | -
  R     M\Security Center | UpdatesDisableNotify | d:1 | -
  R     M\Security Center\Svc | AntiVirusOverride | d:1 | -
  R     M\Security Center\Svc | FirewallOverride | d:1 | -
  R-    CV\Run | SecurityHealth
  R-    CV\Run | WindowsDefender
  R     CV\Explorer\StartupApproved\Run | SecurityHealth | b:030000000000000000000000 | -
  KILL  MsMpEng
  KILL  MpDefenderCoreService
  KILL  NisSrv
  SVCS  4 | WinDefend:2 WdNisSvc:3 SecurityHealthService:2 wscsvc:2 Sense:3 MDCoreSvc:3 MsSecCore:2 MsSecWfp:2 SgrmBroker:2 SgrmAgent:3 wtd:2 webthreatdefusersvc:2 webthreatdefsvc:2 MDCoreSvc_* webthreatdefusersvc_*
  VERIFY WinDefend 4 | Tamper Protection is still on. Open Windows Security > Virus & threat protection > Manage settings, turn off Tamper Protection and Real-time protection, then apply again.
  opt   remove | Remove
  USE   disable
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Settings | UILockDown | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Family options | UILockdown | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Device performance and health | UILockdown | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender Security Center\Account protection | UILockdown | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Spynet | LocalSettingOverrideSpynetReporting | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisableBlockAtFirstSeen | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisableLocalAdminMerge | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender | DisableRoutinelyTakingAction | d:1 | -
  WTDS  ServiceEnabled=0 CaptureThreatWindow=0 NotifyMalicious=0 NotifyPasswordReuse=0 NotifyUnsafeApp=0
  R     CV\WTDS\FeatureFlags | BlockUxDisabled | d:1 | -
  R     CV\WTDS\FeatureFlags | TelemetryCallsEnabled | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender | PassiveMode | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender | IsServiceRunning | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender | PreviousRunningMode | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender | ServiceKeepAlive | d:0 | -
  R     M\Windows Defender | AllowFastServiceStartup | d:0 | -
  R     PM\Windows Defender\Features | TamperProtection | d:0 | -
  SVCS  4 | WdBoot:0 WdFilter:0 WdNisDrv:3 MsSecFlt:0
  DEFSVC WinDefend WdNisSvc SecurityHealthService wscsvc Sense MDCoreSvc MsSecCore MsSecWfp SgrmBroker SgrmAgent wtd webthreatdefsvc webthreatdefusersvc
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\Windows Defender\
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\ExploitGuard\
  A!    Microsoft.SecHealthUI
  A!    *Windows.SecurityCenter*
  DELDIR %ProgramFiles%\Windows Defender
  DELDIR %ProgramFiles%\Windows Defender Advanced Threat Protection
  DELDIR %ProgramFiles(x86)%\Windows Defender
  DELDIR %ProgramData%\Microsoft\Windows Defender
  DELDIR %ProgramData%\Microsoft\Windows Defender Advanced Threat Protection
  DELDIR %ProgramData%\Microsoft\Windows Security Health
  DELDIR %ProgramData%\Microsoft\Scanner
  FEAT  Windows-Defender-Default-Definitions
  VERIFY WinDefend 4 | Tamper Protection blocked the removal. Turn off Tamper Protection and Real-time protection in Windows Security, restart and apply again. Locked files are deleted at the next restart.

tweak win.coinstallers | install_desktop | rec
  name  Auto-installed device apps off
  desc  Stops Windows from running device co-installers when you plug something in, so mice, keyboards and headsets no longer pull in their vendor apps (Razer Synapse, Logitech and others) on their own. Drivers still install normally.
  R     CV\Device Installer | DisableCoInstallers | d:1 | -

tweak win.autorun | usb_off | rec
  name  AutoRun off
  desc  Stops Windows from running programs automatically from USB drives, CDs and network shares when you plug them in.
  R     CV\Policies\Explorer | NoAutorun | d:1 | -
  R     CV\Policies\Explorer | NoDriveTypeAutoRun | d:255 | -
  R     HKU\.DEFAULT\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\AutoplayHandlers | DisableAutoplay | d:1 | -
  R     HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\AutoplayHandlers | DisableAutoplay | d:1 | d:0

tweak win.bitlocker | encrypted | rec
  name  Automatic device encryption off
  desc  Stops Windows from silently encrypting the system drive with BitLocker during setup or after sign-in with a Microsoft account. Does not decrypt drives that are already encrypted.
  R     CC\BitLocker | PreventDeviceEncryption | d:1 | -

tweak win.pslog | terminal | rec
  name  PowerShell logging off
  desc  Turns off PowerShell module and script block logging, which writes every script you run to the event log.
  R     PW\PowerShell\ModuleLogging | EnableModuleLogging | d:0 | -
  R     PW\PowerShell\ScriptBlockLogging | EnableScriptBlockLogging | d:0 | -

tweak win.msaoptional | account_circle | rec
  name  Microsoft account optional
  desc  Lets Store apps that support it work with a local account instead of asking you to sign in with a Microsoft account.
  R     CV\Policies\System | MSAOptional | d:1 | -

tweak win.nomsa | no_accounts | risk2
  name  Block adding Microsoft accounts
  desc  Stops new Microsoft accounts from being added to Windows. Accounts that already sign in with one keep working.
  R     CV\Policies\System | NoConnectedUser | d:1 | -

tweak win.pwexpire | password | rec
  name  Password expiry off
  desc  Stops local account passwords from expiring every 42 days.
  C     net accounts /maxpwage:unlimited
  off:
  C     net accounts /maxpwage:42

tweak win.errormode | error | rec
  name  Hard error pop-ups off
  desc  Logs system hard errors instead of showing blocking pop-up dialogs, so a failing background app cannot freeze your game behind a message box.
  R     CC\Windows | ErrorMode | d:2 | d:0

tweak win.linked | drive_file_move | rec
  name  Mapped drives in admin apps
  desc  Makes network drives you mapped also visible to programs running as administrator.
  R     CV\Policies\System | EnableLinkedConnections | d:1 | -

sub repair | Repair & maintenance

tweak win.repairsvc | build_circle | action rec
  name  Repair core services & boot drivers
  desc  Puts any storage, file system, network and core Windows service that was disabled back to its normal start type, so a too-aggressive tweak can never leave the PC unbootable. Only services that are fully disabled are touched.
  SVCFIX WdBoot=0 WdFilter=0 WdNisDrv=3 cldflt=3 rdbss=1 bam=1 condrv=2 PEAUTH=2 fvevol=0 storqosflt=0 Wof=0 wcifs=1 mrxsmb=1 mrxsmb20=1 srv2=3 UxSms=2 spaceport=0 vdrvroot=0 storflt=0 acpiex=1 Tcpip6=0
  SVCFIX atapi=0 amdsata=0 amdsbs=0 amdxata=0 ebdrv=0 arcsas=0 ItSas35i=0 LSI_SAS=0 LSI_SAS2i=0 LSI_SAS3i=0 stornvme=0 storahci=0 nvstor=0 nvraid=0 iaStorV=0 iaStorAVC=3 msisadrv=0 intelide=0 pciide=0 3ware=0 SiSRaid2=0 SiSRaid4=0 vsmraid=0 VSTXRAID=0
  SVCFIX Schedule=2 EventLog=2 RpcSs=2 RpcEptMapper=2 DcomLaunch=2 Winmgmt=2 Dnscache=2 Dhcp=2 NlaSvc=2 netprofm=3 W32Time=3 VSS=3 msiserver=3 seclogon=3 COMSysApp=3 NetSetupSvc=3 SharedAccess=3 EventSystem=2
  SVCFIX ?hv hvservice=0 Vid=0 hvcrash=0 hyperkbd=1 hypervideo=1 vmbus=0 vmbusroot=0 storvsp=0 netvsc=0 storvsc=0 vidhotplug=3
  SVCCOPY WdFilter WdBoot WdNisDrv atapi amdsata amdxata ebdrv arcsas ItSas35i LSI_SAS LSI_SAS2i LSI_SAS3i stornvme storahci nvstor nvraid iaStorV iaStorAVC msisadrv intelide pciide spaceport vdrvroot storflt hvservice

tweak win.safemode | shield | choice
  name  Next restart
  desc  Choose how Windows starts after the next restart. Safe Mode loads only basic drivers, useful for removing a broken driver. Remember to switch back to Normal.
  opt   normal | Normal
  BCD-  /deletevalue {current} safeboot
  opt   minimal | Safe Mode
  BCD   /set {current} safeboot minimal
  opt   network | Safe Mode with networking
  BCD   /set {current} safeboot network

tweak win.stability | healing | action
  name  Repair display, input & network services
  desc  Sets the display, NVIDIA, font, sensor, pen, touch keyboard, credential vault and network services back to automatic and starts them, resets MPO and GPU scheduling to driver defaults and re-enables virtual network adapters. Use it if something stopped working after tweaking.
  SVCS  2 | NVDisplay.ContainerLocalSystem NvContainerLocalSystem NvContainerNetworkService DispBrokerDesktopSvc DisplayEnhancementService DsmSvc DevQueryBroker VaultSvc FontCache FontCache3.0.0.0 TimeBrokerSvc CDPSvc QWAVE WbioSrvc
  SVCS  2 | TextInputManagementService PenService SensorService SensorDataService SensrSvc swprv ShellHWDetection DeviceAssociationService WlanSvc Wcmsvc NcbService RmSvc Dhcp Dnscache NlaSvc netprofm
  START NVDisplay.ContainerLocalSystem DispBrokerDesktopSvc FontCache TextInputManagementService WlanSvc Dhcp Dnscache NlaSvc
  R-    M\Windows\Dwm | OverlayTestMode
  R-    CC\GraphicsDrivers | HwSchMode
  R-    M\WcmSvc\wifinetworkmanager\config | AutoConnectAllowedOEM
  R-    PW\WcmSvc\GroupPolicy | fMinimizeConnections
  DEVON WAN Miniport *|NDIS Virtual Network Adapter Enumerator|Microsoft Wi-Fi Direct Virtual Adapter|Bluetooth Device (Personal Area Network)|Microsoft RRAS Root Enumerator|Microsoft Kernel Debug Network Adapter|Microsoft Radio Device Enumeration Bus

tweak win.timesync | update | action rec
  name  Sync the clock
  desc  Points Windows Time at pool.ntp.org and syncs now, for an accurate clock in games, TLS and two-factor codes.
  C     net start w32time
  C     w32tm /config /syncfromflags:manual /manualpeerlist:"0.pool.ntp.org 1.pool.ntp.org 2.pool.ntp.org 3.pool.ntp.org" /update
  C     w32tm /resync

tweak win.recovery | healing | action rec
  name  Turn Windows Recovery back on
  desc  Re-enables the Windows Recovery Environment, which other tweak tools often leave broken, so Startup Repair and Reset this PC keep working.
  C     reagentc /enable

tweak win.perfcounters | monitoring | action
  name  Rebuild performance counters
  desc  Rebuilds the performance counter database and resyncs WMI, which fixes Task Manager and monitoring apps that show no CPU or disk data.
  C     lodctr /r
  C     winmgmt /resyncperf

tweak win.gpupdate | policy | action
  name  Apply policies now
  desc  Refreshes Group Policy, so policy tweaks apply without a restart.
  C     gpupdate /force

tweak win.netngen | code | action
  name  Precompile .NET now
  desc  Runs the queued .NET Framework precompilation once, so .NET apps start faster afterwards. Takes a few minutes.
  C     "%SystemRoot%\Microsoft.NET\Framework64\v4.0.30319\ngen.exe" update
  C     "%SystemRoot%\Microsoft.NET\Framework64\v4.0.30319\ngen.exe" executeQueuedItems
  C     "%SystemRoot%\Microsoft.NET\Framework\v4.0.30319\ngen.exe" executeQueuedItems

tweak win.efi | hard_drive | action rec
  name  Hide the EFI partition letter
  desc  Removes the drive letter some tools give to the hidden EFI boot partition, so it disappears from Explorer.
  EFIHIDE

tweak win.setupacct | person_remove | action rec
  name  Remove the setup account
  desc  Deletes the leftover defaultuser0 account that Windows setup sometimes leaves behind.
  C     net user defaultuser0 /delete

sub features | Windows features

tweak win.features | extension_off | rec reboot
  name  Unused enterprise features
  desc  Removes SMB Direct (RDMA), Remote Differential Compression, Work Folders and the WCF 4.5 services, and turns off the App-V client and smart card plug and play, which home PCs never use.
  FEAT  SMBDirect MSRDC-Infrastructure WorkFolders-Client WCF-Services45 WCF-TCP-PortSharing45
  R     M\AppV\Client | Enabled | d:0 | -
  R     PM\AppV\Client | Enabled | d:0 | -
  R     PW\ScPnP | EnableScPnP | d:0 | -

tweak win.taskmaint | event_busy | rec
  name  Maintenance & diagnostic tasks off
  desc  Disables background tasks that run disk, memory and data-integrity diagnostics, WinSAT, registry idle backups, proactive chkdsk scans, troubleshooters, silent disk cleanup, certificate pre-generation and other upkeep you can run by hand.
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Autochk\Proxy
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\DiskDiagnostic\Microsoft-Windows-DiskDiagnosticResolver
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\DiskFootprint\Diagnostics
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\DiskFootprint\StorageSense
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\DiskCleanup\SilentCleanup
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Diagnosis\Scheduled
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Diagnosis\RecommendedTroubleshootingScanner
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Data Integrity Scan\Data Integrity Scan
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Data Integrity Scan\Data Integrity Scan for Crash Recovery
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Data Integrity Scan\Data Integrity Check And Scan
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\StateRepository\MaintenanceTasks
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\BrokerInfrastructure\BgTaskRegistrationMaintenanceTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\ApplicationData\CleanupTemporaryState
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\ApplicationData\DsSvcCleanup
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\UPnP\UPnPHostConfig
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\RemoteAssistance\RemoteAssistanceTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Registry\RegIdleBackup
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\WDI\ResolutionHost
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Chkdsk\ProactiveScan
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\HelloFace\FODCleanupTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\USB\Usb-Notifications
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\SystemUptime\Resume on Boot
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\FileHistory\File History (maintenance mode)
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Maintenance\WinSAT
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\MemoryDiagnostic\ProcessMemoryDiagnosticEvents
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\MemoryDiagnostic\RunFullMemoryDiagnostic
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\MemoryDiagnostic\AutomaticOfflineMemoryDiagnostic
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Power Efficiency Diagnostics\AnalyzeSystem
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\CertificateServicesClient\AikCertEnrollTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\CertificateServicesClient\KeyPreGenTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\SoftwareProtectionPlatform\SvcRestartTaskLogon
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\SoftwareProtectionPlatform\SvcRestartTaskNetwork
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Clip\License Validation
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\SysMain\ResPriStaticDbSync
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\SysMain\WsSwapAssessmentTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\WinINet\CacheTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Windows Filtering Platform\BfeOnServiceStartTypeChange
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\ExploitGuard\ExploitGuard MDM policy Refresh
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\AppxDeploymentClient\UCPD velocity

tweak win.ngen | code | rec
  name  .NET background compilation off
  desc  Stops .NET Framework from recompiling assemblies in the background after updates, which can max out the CPU for minutes.
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\.NET Framework\

tweak win.defragtask | storage
  name  Scheduled drive optimization off
  desc  Disables the weekly Optimize Drives task. On SSDs this also stops the weekly TRIM pass, so run Optimize Drives by hand now and then if you turn this on.
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Defrag\ScheduledDefrag

tweak win.servicingtasks | handyman | risk2
  name  Servicing tasks off
  desc  Disables the component store cleanup, WinRE verification and Workplace Join device sync tasks. Old update files then pile up until you clean them yourself.
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Servicing\StartComponentCleanup
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\RecoveryEnvironment\VerifyWinRE
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Workplace Join\Device-Sync
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Workplace Join\Recovery-Check

tweak win.maintenance | build | rec
  name  Automatic Maintenance off
  desc  Stops the nightly maintenance window that defragments, scans and updates in the background and can wake the PC.
  R     NT\Schedule\Maintenance | MaintenanceDisabled | d:1 | -
  R     PW\Task Scheduler\Maintenance | WakeUp | d:0 | -

tweak win.toasts | notifications_off
  name  App notifications off
  desc  Turns off all toast and tile notifications from apps, including on the lock screen. Do Not Disturb is gentler if you only want quiet while gaming.
  R     UCV\PushNotifications | ToastEnabled | d:0 | d:1
  R     UCV\Notifications\Settings | NOC_GLOBAL_SETTING_TOASTS_ENABLED | d:0 | -
  R     UCV\Notifications\Settings | NOC_GLOBAL_SETTING_ALLOW_TOASTS_ABOVE_LOCK | d:0 | -
  R     UCV\Notifications\Settings | NOC_GLOBAL_SETTING_ALLOW_CRITICAL_TOASTS_ABOVE_LOCK | d:0 | -
  R     HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\PushNotifications | NoToastApplicationNotification | d:1 | -
  R     HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\PushNotifications | NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen | d:1 | -
  R     HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\PushNotifications | NoTileApplicationNotification | d:1 | -

tweak win.wmp | music_note | reboot
  name  Remove legacy Windows Media Player
  desc  Removes the old Windows Media Player and the media playback feature. The new Media Player app is not affected.
  FEAT  WindowsMediaPlayer MediaPlayback

tweak win.printing | print_disabled | risk2 reboot
  name  Printing off
  desc  For PCs that never print: removes print from right-click menus, hides the Printers page, blocks web printing and removes the print, XPS and Print to PDF features. Also see the Print Spooler service.
  R     PM\Windows NT\Printers | DisableHTTPPrinting | d:1 | -
  R     PM\Windows NT\Printers | DisableWebPnPDownload | d:1 | -
  PRINTV image batfile cmdfile docxfile fonfile htmlfile inffile inifile JSEFile otffile pfmfile regfile rtffile ttcfile ttffile txtfile VBEFile VBSFile WSFFile
  SPV   printers
  FEAT  Printing-Foundation-Features Printing-Foundation-InternetPrinting-Client Printing-XPSServices-Features Printing-PrintToPDFServices-Features
  SVCS  4 | Spooler:2 PrintWorkflowUserSvc:3 PrintDeviceConfigurationService:3 PrintScanBrokerService:3 usbprint:3 McpManagementService:3 PrintNotify:3 StiSvc:3
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Printing\PrinterCleanupTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Printing\PrintJobCleanupTask
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Printing\EduPrintProv

tweak win.nosearch | search_off | risk3 reboot
  name  Remove Windows Search
  desc  Removes the search engine feature and disables SearchHost. Start search, Settings search and Explorer search stop working; Open-Shell or Everything are good replacements.
  FEAT  SearchEngine-Client-Package
  SVCS  4 | WSearch:2
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\Shell\IndexerAutomaticMaintenance
  R     UCV\Search | SearchboxTaskbarMode | d:0 | -
  KILL  SearchHost
  FILEOFF %SystemRoot%\SystemApps\MicrosoftWindows.Client.CBS_*\SearchHost.exe

tweak win.legacy | extension_off | rec reboot
  name  Remove legacy Windows features
  desc  Removes SMBv1, Telnet, TFTP, Simple TCP/IP services, PowerShell 2.0, MSMQ, IIS, WAS and the WCF activation components. Old NAS boxes that only speak SMBv1 stop working.
  FEAT  SMB1Protocol SMB1Protocol-Client SMB1Protocol-Server SMB1Protocol-Deprecation TelnetClient TFTP SimpleTCP TIFFIFilter MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2 MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2Root
  FEAT  MSMQ-Container MSMQ-DCOMProxy MSMQ-HTTP MSMQ-Multicast MSMQ-Server MSMQ-Triggers WAS-ConfigurationAPI WAS-NetFxEnvironment WAS-ProcessModel WAS-WindowsActivationService
  FEAT  WCF-HTTP-Activation WCF-HTTP-Activation45 WCF-MSMQ-Activation45 WCF-NonHTTP-Activation WCF-Pipe-Activation45 WCF-TCP-Activation45 Windows-Identity-Foundation IIS-*

tweak win.remoteassist | support_agent | rec
  name  Remote Assistance off
  desc  Turns off Remote Assistance invitations and closes its firewall rules. Quick Assist and Remote Desktop are separate.
  R     CC\Remote Assistance | fAllowToGetHelp | d:0 | d:1
  R     CC\Remote Assistance | fAllowFullControl | d:0 | -
  FWGROUP off | Remote Assistance

tweak win.safemodemsi | build | rec
  name  Installers in Safe Mode
  desc  Lets the Windows Installer service run in Safe Mode, so you can uninstall a broken driver or app from there.
  R     CC\SafeBoot\Minimal\MSIServer |  | s:Service | -
  R     CC\SafeBoot\Network\MSIServer |  | s:Service | -

tweak win.sudo | admin_panel_settings
  name  Sudo for Windows
  desc  Turns on the built-in sudo command in inline mode, so an elevated command runs in the same terminal window.
  R     CV\Sudo | Enabled | d:3 | -

tweak win.wpbt | memory | rec
  name  Firmware-injected programs off
  desc  Stops Windows from running programs that the motherboard firmware drops in at boot (WPBT), the trick some vendors use to force-install their utilities.
  R     CC\Session Manager | DisableWpbtExecution | d:1 | -

sub update | Windows Update

tweak win.wuoff | block | risk3 reboot ti
  name  Windows Update off
  desc  Disables the Windows Update, Update Orchestrator, Medic and Update Health services, so nothing updates at all. You get no security fixes until you turn it back on.
  SVCS  4 | wuauserv:3 UsoSvc:2 WaaSMedicSvc:3 uhssvc:3
  SVCS  3 | BITS:3 DoSvc:2
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate\AU | NoAutoUpdate | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | DoNotConnectToWindowsUpdateInternetLocations | d:1 | -
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\WindowsUpdate\
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\InstallService\
  T     disable \Microsoft\Windows\WaaSMedic\
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\MusUx*
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\UpdateAssistant*
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\Reboot*
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\USO*
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\StartOobe*
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\OobeExpedite
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\WakeToWork
  T     delete \Microsoft\Windows\UpdateOrchestrator\Universal Orchestrator*

tweak win.healthtools | delete_forever | action
  name  Remove Update Health Tools
  desc  Uninstalls Microsoft Update Health Tools, PC Health Check and the Windows Installation Assistant, which exist only to push feature upgrades.
  MSIX  Microsoft Update Health Tools|Windows PC Health Check
  C     msiexec /X{43D501A5-E5E3-46EC-8F33-9E15D2A2CBD5} /qn /norestart
  C     msiexec /X{804A0628-543B-4984-896C-F58BF6A54832} /qn /norestart
  C     "%ProgramFiles(x86)%\WindowsInstallationAssistant\Windows10UpgraderApp.exe" /SunValley /ForceUninstall
  K-    CV\UpdateHealthTools
  K-    CV\rempl
  K-    M\CloudManagedUpdate
  DELDIR %ProgramW6432%\Microsoft Update Health Tools
  DELDIR %ProgramW6432%\PCHealthCheck
  DELDIR %ProgramFiles(x86)%\WindowsInstallationAssistant

tweak win.wumanual | system_update_alt | rec
  name  Manual updates
  desc  Windows Update asks before downloading, never installs on its own, never restarts while you are signed in and leaves the extra Microsoft products channel alone.
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate\AU | AUOptions | d:2 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate\AU | NoAutoRebootWithLoggedOnUsers | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate\AU | AutoInstallMinorUpdates | d:0 | -
  R     HKLM\SOFTWARE\Wow6432Node\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsUpdate\AU | AutoInstallMinorUpdates | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | AllowTemporaryEnterpriseFeatureControl | d:0 | -
  R     CV\WindowsUpdate\Services\Pending\7971f918-a847-4430-9279-4a52d1efe18d | RegisterWithAU | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | AUPowerManagement | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate\AU | NoAUAsDefaultShutdownOption | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | AllowMUUpdateService | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | SetDisablePauseUXAccess | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | DeferFeatureUpdates | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | DeferFeatureUpdatesPeriodInDays | d:30 | -

tweak win.wudrivers | developer_board_off | rec
  name  Drivers from Windows Update off
  desc  Stops Windows Update from replacing the GPU, chipset and other drivers you installed with its own older versions.
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate | d:1 | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | ExcludeWUDriversInQualityUpdate | d:1 | -
  R     CV\DriverSearching | SearchOrderConfig | d:0 | d:1
  R     CV\DriverSearching | DontSearchWindowsUpdate | d:1 | -
  R     UPW\DriverSearching | DriverUpdateWizardWuSearchEnabled | d:0 | -
  R     PW\Device Metadata | PreventDeviceMetadataFromNetwork | d:1 | -

tweak win.wuux | notifications_off | rec
  name  Update nags off
  desc  Hides restart-required notifications, the "new version of Windows" upgrade banner, the Media Creation Tool link, and blocks Store-delivered OS upgrades.
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | RestartNotificationsAllowed2 | d:0 | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | HideMCTLink | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | UpdateNotificationLevel | d:2 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | HideMCTLink | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | RestartNotificationsAllowed2 | d:0 | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | TrayIconVisibility | d:0 | -
  R     HKLM\SYSTEM\Setup\UpgradeNotification | UpgradeAvailable | d:0 | -
  R     PM\WindowsStore | DisableOSUpgrade | d:1 | -

tweak win.wupause | pause_circle | risk2
  name  Pause updates
  desc  Pauses feature and quality updates until 2033 and allows pauses up to 10 years in Settings. You get no security fixes while paused, so resume now and then.
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | FlightSettingsMaxPauseDays | d:3650 | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseFeatureUpdatesStartTime | s:2025-01-01T00:00:00Z | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseFeatureUpdatesEndTime | s:2033-01-01T00:00:00Z | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseQualityUpdatesStartTime | s:2025-01-01T00:00:00Z | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseQualityUpdatesEndTime | s:2033-01-01T00:00:00Z | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseUpdatesStartTime | s:2025-01-01T00:00:00Z | -
  R     M\WindowsUpdate\UX\Settings | PauseUpdatesExpiryTime | s:2033-01-01T00:00:00Z | -

tweak win.insider | science | rec
  name  Insider builds & experiments off
  desc  Blocks Windows Insider preview builds, configuration flighting and the feature experiments Microsoft runs on normal PCs, and hides the Insider page in Settings.
  R     M\WindowsSelfHost\UI\Visibility | HideInsiderPage | d:1 | -
  R     PW\PreviewBuilds | AllowBuildPreview | d:0 | -
  R     PW\PreviewBuilds | EnableConfigFlighting | d:0 | -
  R     PW\PreviewBuilds | EnableExperimentation | d:0 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | ManagePreviewBuilds | d:1 | -
  R     PW\WindowsUpdate | ManagePreviewBuildsPolicyValue | d:0 | -

tweak win.appupdates | update_disabled | rec
  name  App auto-updates off
  desc  Stops the Microsoft Store and Windows Media Player from updating apps on their own. You can still update from the Store's Library page.
  R     PM\WindowsStore | AutoDownload | d:2 | -
  R     PM\WindowsStore | DisableStoreAppsAutoUpdate | d:1 | -
  R     CV\WindowsStore\WindowsUpdate | AutoDownload | d:2 | -
  R     PM\WindowsMediaPlayer | DisableAutoUpdate | d:1 | -

tweak win.arso | key_off | rec
  name  Auto sign-in after updates off
  desc  Stops Windows from using your saved sign-in to finish setting up the account after an update restart.
  R     CV\Policies\System | DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn | d:1 | -
